  "caveats": [
    "Observational: TE alignment is chosen by the offense, partly in response to expected defense; residuals are associations, not causal effects.",
    "Context model omits TE count/alignment by design, so personnel-driven differences (e.g. 12 vs 11 personnel) are partly absorbed via n_rb/n_wr/n_detached_nonte.",
    "No-TE plays are rare (~3%) so no-TE and team-level no-TE estimates are noisy; most teams have < 20 no-TE plays (see n_no_te in teams.csv).",
    "Data are dropbacks only (no designed runs), weeks 1-8 of 2021.",
    "defendersInBox is a PFF/NGS pre-snap label; deep counts use snap-frame tracking (x_rel >= 10), which misses late rotation after the snap.",
    "Player value is a within-player inline-vs-detached contrast; low reliability means it mostly reflects scheme/opponent noise rather than a stable player trait."
  ],
